IMPORT prelude

-- Prevention of Corruption Act 1960 (2020 Revised Edition), Singapore Statutes Online, current version as at 01 Oct 2026.
-- Source: source/PCA1960.txt (extracted from source/PCA1960.pdf); the line references in the other modules are to that file.
--
-- The shared nouns, and nothing else: DECLARE only, no rules, no #EVAL.  Every rule module imports this one.
--
-- Membership test: could a witness of ordinary competence testify to this fact, or does answering it require reading the Act?  Only
-- the first kind is a field here.  "The accused solicited a gratification" is a fact; "the accused is guilty of an offence under
-- section 5(a)" is a rule.  Where the Act itself names an element that is a conclusion of law (the thing is "a gratification", the
-- person is "an agent"), the facts that decide it are fields and the conclusion is a rule in pca-offences.l4.
--
-- SCOPE: every operative provision of Parts 1, 3, 4, 5 and 6 (offences, the penalty rules, the presumption, the investigation and arrest
-- powers, the evidence rules, and the procedural sections).  Part 2 sections 3 and 4 (appointment; officers deemed public servants) are
-- encoded; sections 4A to 4F (the Occupational Superannuation Scheme of CPIB officers) are pension administration with no bearing on a
-- prosecution and are not encoded.  NOTES.md section 2 is the coverage table.

§ `Part 1. What the Act's own words name: gratification, agent`

@ref "Prevention of Corruption Act 1960, s 2 'gratification' (a) to (e)"
DECLARE `Gratification Facts` HAS
    `the thing is money or a gift, loan, fee, reward, commission, valuable security or other property or interest in property of any description, movable or immovable` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the thing is an office, employment or contract` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the thing is a payment, release, discharge or liquidation of a loan, obligation or other liability whatsoever, in whole or in part` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the thing is any other service, favour or advantage of any description whatsoever, including protection from a penalty or disability or from disciplinary or penal action, or the exercise or the forbearance from the exercise of a right or an official power or duty` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the thing is an offer, undertaking or promise of anything within the other four paragraphs` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref "Prevention of Corruption Act 1960, s 2 'agent'"
DECLARE `Agency Facts` HAS
    `the person was employed by or acting for another` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person was a trustee, administrator or executor` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person was serving the Government or was under a corporation or public body` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person was a subcontractor, or employed by or acting for a subcontractor` IS A BOOLEAN

§ `Part 3. Offences`

@ref "Prevention of Corruption Act 1960, s 5(a) and (b)"
DECLARE `Section 5 Facts` HAS
    `the accused solicited or received, or agreed to receive, a gratification for himself or herself or for any other person` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the accused gave, promised or offered a gratification to any person, whether for the benefit of that person or of another person` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the accused acted corruptly` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the gratification was an inducement to, reward for, or on account of, any person doing or forbearing to do anything in respect of any matter or transaction whatsoever, actual or proposed` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the gratification was an inducement to, reward for, or on account of, a member, officer or servant of a public body doing or forbearing to do anything in respect of any matter or transaction whatsoever, actual or proposed, in which the public body is concerned` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref "Prevention of Corruption Act 1960, s 6(a), (b) and (c)"
DECLARE `Section 6 Facts` HAS
    `the agent accepted or obtained, or agreed to accept or attempted to obtain, from any person, a gratification for himself or herself or for any other person` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the accused gave, agreed to give or offered a gratification to an agent` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the accused acted corruptly` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the gratification was an inducement or reward for doing or forbearing to do, or for having done or forborne to do, an act in relation to the principal's affairs or business, or for showing or forbearing to show favour or disfavour to any person in relation to the principal's affairs or business` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the accused knowingly gave an agent a receipt, account or other document` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the accused, being an agent, knowingly used with intent to deceive the principal a receipt, account or other document` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the principal is interested in the document` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the document contains a statement which is false or erroneous or defective in a material particular` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the statement is, to the accused's knowledge, intended to mislead the principal` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref "Prevention of Corruption Act 1960, s 7"
DECLARE `Government Contract Facts` HAS
    `the matter or transaction was a contract or a proposal for a contract with the Government or any department of the Government` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the matter or transaction was a contract or a proposal for a contract with a public body` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the matter or transaction was a subcontract to execute work comprised in such a contract` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref "Prevention of Corruption Act 1960, s 8"
DECLARE `Presumption Facts` HAS
    `the gratification was paid or given to, or received by, a person in the employment of the Government or any department of the Government or of a public body` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the gratification was paid or given by, or received from, a person who has or seeks to have any dealing with the Government or any department of the Government or any public body` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the gratification was paid or given by, or received from, an agent of a person who has or seeks to have any dealing with the Government or any department of the Government or any public body` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the contrary is proved` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref "Prevention of Corruption Act 1960, s 9(1) and (2)"
DECLARE `Section 9 Facts` HAS
    `the agent corruptly accepted, obtained or agreed to accept, or attempted to obtain, a gratification` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the accused corruptly gave, agreed to give or offered a gratification to an agent` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the accused had reason to believe or suspect that the gratification was offered as an inducement or reward for doing or forbearing to do an act, or for showing or forbearing to show favour or disfavour to a person, in relation to the principal's affairs or business` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the accused had reason to believe or suspect that the agent had the power, right or opportunity to do, show or forbear, and that the act, favour or disfavour was in relation to the principal's affairs or business` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the agent had the power, right or opportunity to do, show or forbear` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the agent accepted the gratification without intending to do, show or forbear` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the agent did not in fact do, show or forbear` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the act, favour or disfavour was not in relation to the principal's affairs or business` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref "Prevention of Corruption Act 1960, s 10(a) and (b)"
DECLARE `Section 10 Facts` HAS
    `the accused offered a gratification to a person who had made a tender for a contract` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the accused did so with intent to obtain the contract from the Government or a public body` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the contract was for performing work, providing a service, doing anything, or supplying an article, material or substance` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the gratification was an inducement or a reward for the tenderer's withdrawing the tender` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the accused solicited or accepted a gratification as an inducement or a reward for withdrawing a tender made by the accused for that contract` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref "Prevention of Corruption Act 1960, s 11(a) and (b)"
DECLARE `Section 11 Facts` HAS
    `the accused offered a gratification to a Member of Parliament` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the accused, being a Member of Parliament, solicited or accepted a gratification` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the gratification was an inducement or reward for the Member's doing or forbearing to do an act in his or her capacity as a Member` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref "Prevention of Corruption Act 1960, s 12(a) and (b)"
DECLARE `Section 12 Facts` HAS
    `the accused offered a gratification to a member of a public body` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the accused, being a member of a public body, solicited or accepted a gratification` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the gratification was an inducement or reward for the member's voting or abstaining from voting at a meeting of the public body in favour of or against a measure, resolution or question submitted to it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the gratification was an inducement or reward for the member's performing or abstaining from performing, or aid in procuring, expediting, delaying, hindering or preventing the performance of, an official act` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the gratification was an inducement or reward for the member's aid in procuring or preventing the passing of a vote or the granting of a contract or advantage in favour of any person` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref "Prevention of Corruption Act 1960, ss 29, 30 and 31"
DECLARE `Inchoate Offence Facts` HAS
    `the accused abetted, within the meaning of the Penal Code 1871, the commission of an offence under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the accused abetted, within the meaning of the Penal Code 1871, the commission outside Singapore of an act, in relation to the affairs or business or on behalf of a principal residing in Singapore, which if committed in Singapore would be an offence under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the accused attempted to commit an offence punishable under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the accused was a party to a criminal conspiracy, within the meaning of the Penal Code 1871, to commit an offence under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN

§ `Part 3. Which offence, and its punishment`

@ref "Prevention of Corruption Act 1960, ss 5, 6, 10, 11, 12, 18(2), 21(2), 26, 28, 32(2) and the penalty provisions of each"
DECLARE `Offence under the Act` IS ONE OF
    `Corruption by soliciting or receiving (section 5(a))`
    `Corruption by giving, promising or offering (section 5(b))`
    `Agent accepting or obtaining a gratification (section 6(a))`
    `Giving a gratification to an agent (section 6(b))`
    `False receipt, account or document given to or used by an agent (section 6(c))`
    `Offering a gratification for the withdrawal of a tender (section 10(a))`
    `Soliciting or accepting a gratification for withdrawing a tender (section 10(b))`
    `Offering a gratification to a Member of Parliament (section 11(a))`
    `Member of Parliament soliciting or accepting a gratification (section 11(b))`
    `Offering a gratification to a member of a public body (section 12(a))`
    `Member of a public body soliciting or accepting a gratification (section 12(b))`
    `Failure to disclose information or produce documents to an authorised person (section 18(2))`
    `Failure to comply with a notice of the Public Prosecutor (section 21(2))`
    `Obstruction of search and failure to give information (section 26)`
    `False or misleading information (section 28)`
    `Public officer failing to arrest the giver of a gratification (section 32(2))`

@ref "Prevention of Corruption Act 1960, the punishment clause of each offence section; section 7"
DECLARE `Corruption Punishment` HAS
    `the maximum fine in dollars` IS A NUMBER
    `the maximum imprisonment in months` IS A NUMBER

@ref "Prevention of Corruption Act 1960, s 13(1) and (2)"
DECLARE `Section 13 Facts` HAS
    `the person is convicted of an offence committed by the acceptance of a gratification in contravention of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the gratification is a sum of money` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the value of the gratification can be assessed` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the amount of the gratification, or in the court's opinion its value, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
    `the other offences taken into consideration under section 148 of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010 were offences for the acceptance of gratification in contravention of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the total amount or value of the gratification specified in the charges for the offences taken into consideration, in dollars` IS A NUMBER

@ref "Prevention of Corruption Act 1960, s 14"
DECLARE `Section 14 Facts` HAS
    `a gratification has, in contravention of this Act, been given by a person to an agent` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the defendant is the agent or the person who gave the gratification` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the plaintiff is the principal` IS A BOOLEAN

§ `Parts 4 and 6. The offences about investigations and information`

@ref "Prevention of Corruption Act 1960, ss 18(2), 21(1) and (2)"
DECLARE `Investigation Offence Facts` HAS
    `an order of the Public Prosecutor under section 18(1) authorises the officer to investigate and to require disclosure or production` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the accused failed to disclose the information or to produce the accounts, documents or articles to the person so authorised` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a written notice of the Public Prosecutor under section 21(1) was sent to the accused in the course of an investigation or proceedings into an offence by a person in the service of the Government or of a department or of a public body` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the offence investigated is an offence under this Act or under sections 161 to 165 or 213 to 215 of the Penal Code 1871, or a conspiracy to commit, attempt to commit or abetment of one` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the accused wilfully neglected or failed to comply with the notice within the time specified in it` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref "Prevention of Corruption Act 1960, s 26(a) to (d)"
DECLARE `Section 26 Facts` HAS
    `the accused refused the Director or an officer authorised to enter or search access to a place` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the accused assaulted, obstructed, hindered or delayed the Director or an officer in effecting an entrance he or she is entitled to effect under the Act, or in the execution of a duty or power under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the accused failed to comply with a lawful demand of the Director or an officer in the execution of his or her duty under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the accused refused or neglected to give information which might reasonably be required of him or her and which he or she had it in his or her power to give` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref "Prevention of Corruption Act 1960, s 28(a) and (b)"
DECLARE `Section 28 Facts` HAS
    `the accused knowingly gave or caused to be given false or misleading information relating to the commission of an offence under this Act or under section 165, 213, 214 or 215 of the Penal Code 1871` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the accused knowingly gave or caused to be given to the Director or a special investigator any other false or misleading information` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref "Prevention of Corruption Act 1960, s 32(2)"
DECLARE `Section 32(2) Facts` HAS
    `a gratification was corruptly given or offered to the public officer` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the public officer arrested the person who gave or offered the gratification and made the person over to the nearest police station` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the public officer had a reasonable excuse for not doing so` IS A BOOLEAN

§ `Part 4. Arrest, bail, investigation, search`

@ref "Prevention of Corruption Act 1960, ss 3, 4(1), 15(1), 16(1), 17(1), 19, 22"
DECLARE `Officer Role` IS ONE OF
    `the Director of the Corrupt Practices Investigation Bureau`
    `a deputy director`
    `an assistant director`
    `a special investigator`
    `a police officer of or above the rank of assistant superintendent`
    `a police officer not below the rank of inspector but below assistant superintendent`
    `another police officer`
    `a Magistrate`
    `some other person`

@ref "Prevention of Corruption Act 1960, s 15(1)"
DECLARE `Arrest Facts` HAS
    `the person has been concerned in an offence under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a reasonable complaint has been made against the person of having been so concerned` IS A BOOLEAN
    `credible information has been received that the person was so concerned` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a reasonable suspicion exists of the person's having been so concerned` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person arrested is a female` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the searcher is a female` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref "Prevention of Corruption Act 1960, s 17(1)"
DECLARE `Investigation Power Facts` HAS
    `the case relates to an offence under section 165 or sections 213 to 215 of the Penal Code 1871, or to a conspiracy, attempt or abetment of one` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the case relates to an offence under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the case relates to an arrestable offence under a written law which may be disclosed in the course of an investigation under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Public Prosecutor has ordered the investigation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Public Prosecutor is satisfied that there are reasonable grounds for suspecting that an offence under this Act has been committed` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Public Prosecutor considers that evidence of an offence under this Act or under sections 161 to 165 or 213 to 215 of the Penal Code 1871, or of a conspiracy, attempt or abetment of one, by a person in the service of the Government or of a department or of a public body is likely to be found in a banker's book` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the banker's book relates to that person, to his wife or child, or to a person reasonably believed by the Public Prosecutor to be a trustee or agent for that person` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref "Prevention of Corruption Act 1960, s 27"
DECLARE `Section 27 Facts` HAS
    `the person was required by the Director or an officer to give information` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the information is on a subject which it is the duty of the Director or that officer to inquire into under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is in the person's power to give the information` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref "Prevention of Corruption Act 1960, s 22(1) and (2)"
DECLARE `Search Facts` HAS
    `it appears upon information and after such inquiry as the Magistrate or the Director thinks necessary that there is reasonable cause to believe that in a place there is a document containing evidence of, or an article or property relating to, an offence under this Act, or under sections 161 to 165 or 213 to 215 of the Penal Code 1871, or a conspiracy, attempt or abetment of one` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the special investigator or police officer has reasonable cause to believe that such a document, article or property is concealed or deposited in the place` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the special investigator or police officer has reasonable grounds for believing that by reason of the delay in obtaining a search warrant the object of the search is likely to be frustrated` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a warrant has been issued by a Magistrate or the Director, directed to the searcher` IS A BOOLEAN

§ `Part 5. Evidence`

@ref "Prevention of Corruption Act 1960, ss 23, 24, 25, 36"
DECLARE `Corruption Evidence Facts` HAS
    `the proceeding is a civil or criminal proceeding under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the evidence is offered to show that a gratification mentioned in the Act is customary in a profession, trade, vocation or calling` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the trial or inquiry is into an offence under this Act or under sections 161 to 165 or 213 to 215 of the Penal Code 1871, or into a conspiracy, attempt or abetment of one` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the accused is in possession of pecuniary resources or property disproportionate to his or her known sources of income for which he or she cannot satisfactorily account` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the accused obtained at or about the time of the alleged offence an accretion to pecuniary resources or property for which he or she cannot satisfactorily account` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the resources, property or accretion are held or obtained by another person` IS A BOOLEAN
    `there is reason to believe, having regard to that person's relationship to the accused or to other circumstances, that the other person holds them in trust for or on behalf of the accused or as a gift from the accused` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the witness paid or delivered, or had paid or delivered on his or her behalf, a gratification to an agent or a member of a public body` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the proceeding is a trial for an offence under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the informer wilfully made in his or her complaint a material statement which he or she knew or believed to be false or did not believe to be true, and the court, after full inquiry into the case, is of that opinion` IS A BOOLEAN
    `in a proceeding that is not a trial for an offence under this Act, the court is of the opinion that justice cannot be fully done between the parties without the discovery of the informer` IS A BOOLEAN

§ `Part 6. Procedure: consent, court, examination, extraterritorial reach`

@ref "Prevention of Corruption Act 1960, ss 32(1), 33, 34, 35, 37"
DECLARE `Procedure Facts` HAS
    `the prosecution is instituted by the Public Prosecutor` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the prosecution is instituted with the consent of the Public Prosecutor` IS A BOOLEAN
    `two or more persons are charged with an offence under this Act or under sections 161 to 165 or 213 to 215 of the Penal Code 1871, or with a conspiracy, attempt or abetment of one` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person was required by the court under section 35(1) to give evidence as a witness for the prosecution` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person required to give evidence in the opinion of the court makes true and full discovery of all things as to which he or she is lawfully examined` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the accused is a citizen of Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the offence under this Act was committed in a place outside Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
